      "text": "Given the recurrence relation:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_{n-1} a_{n+1}\n\\]\n\nwe can rearrange it to find:\n\n\\[\na_{n+1} = \\frac{a_n}{a_{n-1}}\n\\]\n\nLet's denote the sequence parameters \\(\\{a_n\\}\\) as:\n\n\\[\na_0, a_1, a_2, \\ldots\n\\]\n\nSince:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_0 \\frac{a_1}{a_0} \\frac{a_2}{a_1} \\cdots \\frac{a_n}{a_{n-1}}\n\\]\n\nit implies:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_{n-1} \\frac{a_n}{a_{n-1}} = \\frac{a_n}{a_0}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(a_n\\) yields:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_{n-1} \\frac{a_n}{a_{n-1}} = a_{n-1} \\left(\\frac{a_n}{a_0}\\right)\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_n (\\frac{a_n}{a_0})\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\na_1 = a_0 a_1 \\Leftrightarrow a_0 = 1\n\\]\n\nWe know:\n\n\\[\na_1 = 1 + \\sqrt{7}\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_0 \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{7}}{a_1} \\frac{a_n}{a_0} \\Rightarrow a_n = \\frac{(1 + \\sqrt{7})a_n}{a_1}\n\\]\n\nSolving the equation:\n\n\\[\na_n a_1 = (1 + \\sqrt{7})a_n \\Rightarrow a_n = (1 + \\sqrt{7})a_{n-1} \\quad \\text{for} \\quad n \\ge 2\n\\]\n\nWe observe:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_{n-1} (1 + \\sqrt{7})\n\\]\nwhich implies:\n\n\\[\na_n = a_1 (1 + \\sqrt{7})^{n-1}\n\\]\n\nGiven \\(a_1 = 1 + \\sqrt{7}\\):\n\n\\[\na_1 = 2^{-s_1} (1 + \\sqrt{7})^{s_1} = 13 + \\sqrt{7}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to show:\n\n\\[\ns_1 + s_2 + \\cdots + s_n = ns - 2009\n\\]\n\nRewriting \\(s_i\\) terms:\n\n\\[\ns_n = t = \\frac{n^2 - 3n + 5}{2} - \\frac{7n + 3}{2} = \\frac{(n-1)^2 - n + 2}{2} = n - \\frac{n}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} = n - \\frac{n}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} = 2(n-1) = -2 + 2(n-1)\n\\]\n\nThen:\n\n\\[\ns_i = s_0 + i - 1 + 1 = -2009\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\ns_0 = -2010 \\quad \\text{we get} \\quad a_{2009}= (a_0) 13 + \\sqrt{7}\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[\na_{2009} = \\boxed{13 + \\sqrt{7}}\n\\]",
